{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation note: the complexity ratchet keys accepted debt by `path::symbol`, so moving `_scan` (ceiling 27) and `_check_snapshot` (ceiling 16) out of `fsck.py` reads to `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py` as 2 new findings + 2 stale ones. Re-keyed both to `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py::` at their **identical existing ceilings** — no ceiling raised, no debt added (`--check` now reports `new=0 increased=0 stale=0`). Added `.github/complexity-baseline.json` to the declared file impact.\n\nMeasured result: fsck.py 800 -> 301, fsck_scan.py 317, fsck_tracker_health.py 235. All three inside the 200-500 target band, none under the 100 floor. No test file edited; 900 passed across the fsck/store/lifecycle suites."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786600804669744001,"uuid":"23262b71-7edc-4910-b6e0-f58e7d654bfb"}